// e2e/ is not in tsconfig.json's `include`, so `tsc --noEmit` never saw it: a
// spec could read a property that does not exist and the gate stayed green
// until Playwright hit `undefined` at runtime. That happened -- overflow.ts's
// return property was renamed and the four call sites in responsive.spec.ts
// and sheet-responsive.spec.ts were not, `typecheck` passed, and 34 e2e
// checks failed in the browser (#266).
//
// A second program rather than adding "e2e" to the main `include`: the specs
// need Node types (process.env in session.integration.spec.ts) that app code
// must not have, and widening the app program to get them would hand `process`
// to every module under src/ -- the app bundle has no Node, so those types
// would only ever be wrong there.
//
// `extends` rather than a standalone config so strict, noUncheckedIndexedAccess
// and noUnusedLocals stay in one place. They are load-bearing here: a config
// that merely parsed the directory would add a passing step and catch nothing.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // DOM comes from the base `lib` and is needed inside page.evaluate, whose
    // callback really does run in the browser. "node" replaces the base's
    // vitest/globals, which the specs do not use -- Playwright's `test` and
    // `expect` are imported, not global.
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["e2e"]
}
